MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AUDIT: InvestigationState.add_hypothesis appends without dedup, and
finding-level keying lives entirely in proposer-minted hypothesis_ids
— no deterministic identity-scope mechanism existed, so nothing
prevents security-distinct investigations from collapsing onto one id
or logically identical ones duplicating on representation noise.

IMPLEMENTATION (src/webpent/egaie/identity_scope.py):
  * IdentityContext over the directive's twelve dimensions (actor,
    role, tenant, namespace, resource ownership, object identity,
    operation, workflow state, session, auth strength, HTTP method,
    preconditions) — presence vs absence of a dimension is itself a
    distinction (unauthenticated != authenticated);
  * identity_scope_key: stable sha256 fingerprint over a canonical
    form; representation-only details (request ids, idempotency
    tokens, nonces, timestamps, query order) are stripped at
    construction and can never split identical hypotheses;
  * compare_identity_scope/explain: every decision carries a reason
    and the exact differing fields;
  * deduplicate_hypotheses: groups by (family, scope) — deterministic
    (smallest id kept), bounded report, unknown contexts never merge;
  * state semantics deliberately untouched — dedup is an explicit,
    reportable operation, never silent loss mid-investigation.

TESTS (tests/test_umdr43_identity_scope.py, 11/11): both mandatory
directive regression cases pinned (genuine duplicates merge;
security-distinct hypotheses stay separate), fingerprint stability,
bounded reporting. Existing egaie suites unaffected (module is additive).
